      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Listen, I'm not going to sugarcoat it, the ER bill is a real concern, but your life is worth more than a few grand. The shortness of breath is a sign that the clot is breaking loose and could be life-threatening. Aspirin and sleep aren't going to fix this, and you need to get it checked out ASAP. I'm not saying you should ignore it, but I am saying you need to take a deep breath and prioritize your health over your wallet. If you're really worried about the cost, you can always try to get a second opinion or negotiate with the hospital, but don't wait until it's too late.",
